highlights_Qualifications:
Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or related field (willing to accept foreign education equivalent) plus five (5) years of experience as a Quality Automation Engineer (SDET) or related occupation in software QA automation or software development
Or, alternatively, a Master's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or related field and three (3) years of experience as a Quality Automation Engineer (SDET) or related occupation in software QA automation or software development
Specific skills/other requirements - Must also possess the following (quantitative experience requirements not applicable to this section):
Performing test automation using Java, JavaScript, Python, or SQL/NoSQL;
Building automation test frameworks using Selenium, TestNG, RestAssured, or Intuit;
Karate, Cucumber, Allure Reporting, Mockito, Splunk, Jmeter, or AppDynamics;
Jenkins, Confluence, or Jira for full testing life cycle;
Load, fail-over, fault-tolerance, or chaos testing, as well as conducting performance tests, including 2 of the following: capacity, load, or soak testing; and
At least 3 of the following observability tools: AppDynamics, Lighthouse, Datadog, DPA, Splunk, or GCP stack driver

Degree required: Bachelor's degree in Electronic Engineering, or related technical field
Amount and type of experience required: 4 years of experience in the job offered or in a related position involving software engineering experience
4 years of hands-on experience in Hadoop;
4 years of experience with MongoDB;
3 years of experience with Python or Unix/Shell scripting or Spark;
3 years of experience with Autosys;
2 years of experience with Dremio;
2 years of experience in setting up monitoring dashboards through Grafana or Prometheus;
1 year of experience with Kubernetes; and
1 year of experience with Azure or GCP
Third-Party recordings are prohibited unless authorized by Wells Fargo
Wells Fargo requires you to directly represent your own experiences during the recruiting and hiring process

